   "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
   "body_html": "<p>You likely forgot to <code>#include &lt;stdlib.h&gt;</code></p>\n"
  },
  {
   "post_type": "answer",
   "post_id": 7050808,
   "parent_id": 7050798,
   "author_user_id": 484899,
   "author_display_name": "Antti",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/7050808",
   "score": 16,
   "created_utc": "2011-08-13T13:51:16Z",
   "last_edit_utc": null,
   "last_activity_utc": "2011-08-13T13:51:16Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p>You're missing <code>#include &lt;stdlib.h&gt;</code>.</p>\n"
  },
  {
   "post_type": "answer",
   "post_id": 7050809,
   "parent_id": 7050798,
   "author_user_id": 111886,
   "author_display_name": "Omri Barel",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/7050809",
   "score": 48,
   "created_utc": "2011-08-13T13:51:18Z",
   "last_edit_utc": "2017-12-10T21:37:36Z",
   "last_activity_utc": "2017-12-10T21:37:36Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p>You need to <code>#include &lt;stdlib.h&gt;</code>. Otherwise it's defined as <code>int malloc()</code> which is incompatible with the built-in type <code>void *malloc(size_t)</code>.</p>\n"
  },
